    "result_text": "The full test suite is green: **256 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `contactPreference` = `'EMAIL'` when an email is present, otherwise `'PHONE'`, on the owner API response.\n\nTwo changes, following the codebase's existing pattern for derived owner fields (like `locality`, `membershipLevel`):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `contactPreference` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` includes the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` with a `contactPreference(owner)` helper that returns `\"EMAIL\"` when the owner has a non-blank email, otherwise `\"PHONE\"`.\n\nThe value flows through the existing `RespondWithOwner` OfficeFloor function and the mapper into every owner response (GET `/api/owners/{ownerId}` is what the tests hit). Both new acceptance tests (`corePhoneWhenNoEmail`, `functionalityEmailWhenPresent`) pass, and all 256 tests remain green.\n\nI used a plain `type: string` rather than an inline enum to keep the mapper expression simple and consistent with the sibling `locality` field, avoiding a generated nested enum type.",
